## Writing Principles
- Simple, succinct, technical, factual
- Active voice, concrete examples, consistent terminology
- 300-500 words/section, remove redundancy

## Content Structure
- Most important information first
- Clear headings, one concept per section
- Link related pages at end (optional)
- Page structure: Title/description → short intro → Main content (H2/H3) → Examples → Related links (when relevant)

## Navigation
- Max 5-7 top categories, max 2 levels deep
- Breadcrumb-friendly, bidirectional links, search-optimized

## Organization
- DRY, progressive complexity (simple → advanced)
- Task-based guides, separate reference from tutorials, modular

## Layers
- This MDX is canonical **technical** docs (architecture, ADRs, how-to). Product intent lives in `_first/basilic/PRODUCT.md`, not Fumadocs. Rules do not `@`-attach MDX
- READMEs are how to run the app/package; they link here, no duplication
- Update this page when behavior, architecture, commands, or conventions change (same change as the code)
